# Use State from TypeScript

Declare state inside an app or device participant. Define its schema model in
the implemented API; the generator derives the required state runtime grants.
Services use KV resources instead of participant state.

```trellis
state preferences value {
  schema Preferences;
  state_version "preferences.v1";
}
```

Run `trellis generate` and connect with the generated participant. For a
`Preferences` model containing `theme: string`:

```ts
await client.state.preferences.put({ theme: "dark" }).orThrow();
const stored = await client.state.preferences.get().orThrow();
if ("found" in stored && stored.found) {
  console.log(stored.entry.value.theme);
}
```

State belongs to the stable principal and participant lineage, not a socket.
It survives reconnects and server restarts. Use the revision/CAS options exposed
by the generated handle when coordinating concurrent writes. A `state_version`
change is a migration decision, not a cache-busting value. Never access the
internal state bucket directly.
